speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, I am dealing with energy, including energy developed from water. That is clause 8, and that is the very thing I am dealing with. I want to

know how this is going to fit into the national grid. This question was raised the other day in the debate. Nothing could tie in more closely than hydro power. We are not talking about the establishment of a new department; we are talking about clause 8, which reads in part:
(a)	energy, including energy developed from water;
(b)	mines and minerals and other non-renewable resources;
And so on down the line. I ask hon. members to read the section. My question to the minister is: What rules are being made to establish this national grid, and just where does the department stand with respect to it at this time?
